# How to cite RoboARC. Title, authors and their order are the paper's. `version` and `date-released` are those of the
# task set (CHANGELOG.md). The paper is arXiv 2611.33390; keep README.md's BibTeX entry the same.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RoboARC in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "RoboARC: Physical Puzzles for Robotic Manipulation under Spatial Constraints"
abstract: >-
  RoboARC is a benchmark of physical puzzles for robotic manipulation under spatial constraints: 90 tasks in six
  constraint types over rigid and soft materials, on three robots in MuJoCo. Every task is a frozen scene with a
  physics-based grader and a verified reference solution, in a Privileged mode with the full simulator state and
  resets and a Standard mode with camera images, proprioception and a single attempt.
